                                                                       ] ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "Weathering Rock refers to the process of rock decomposition due to environmental factors like temperature changes, water, and chemical reactions. This process is important in soil formation as it contributes to the breakdown of parent material into smaller particles that form soil. Source: AGI, 'Encyclopedia of Geology'" ;
